---
title: Lemon Meringue Tart
cooklang: 2
servings: 8
makes: one 23 cm tart
course: dessert
allergens: [egg, dairy, gluten]
tags: [tart, citrus, make ahead]
---

= Shell ~{-1%day} -> shell

`Line` a #23 cm tart tin{} with @./Bases/Shortcrust{350%g}, prick the base, and rest in the
#fridge{} for ~rest{30%minutes}.

`Blind bake uncovered 180 °C` with #baking paper{} and #baking beans{} at 180 °C for ~oven{15%minutes}, then
~oven{10%minutes} uncovered until ~{pale gold}.

= Curd -> curd

`Whisk` @lemon zest{1%tbsp} and @lemon juice{120%ml}(from 3 lemons) with
@caster sugar{150%g}, @egg yolks{4} and @whole eggs{2} in a #heavy saucepan{}.

`Cook medium-low` over medium-low heat, stirring constantly, ~{8-10%minutes} until ~{thick enough to coat the spoon}. Do not let it boil.

`Beat in off ×` @unsalted butter{80%g}(cubed, cold) a piece at a time off the heat.

`Fill` the @&shell{} in the #&23 cm tart tin{} with the @&curd{} and `chill` ~rest{2%hours}.

= Meringue

`Whisk` @egg whites{4} in a #clean bowl{} with a #stand mixer{}|#electric whisk{} to soft
peaks, then `add ×` @caster sugar{200%g} a spoon at a time to stiff, glossy peaks. -> meringue

`Spread` the @&meringue{} over the @&shell{}, sealing to the edge. Swirl with a #spoon{}.

`Brown` under the #grill{} for ~{2-3%minutes}, or with a #?blowtorch{}, until ~{the peaks colour}. Watch it: it turns in seconds.

`Garnish?` with @?lemon zest{}(a few strands) and serve within a day.
